<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tegernsee Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century–1803</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tegernsee Abbey was a Benedictine monastery on the Tegernsee lake in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-bavaria">Upper Bavaria</a>, founded in the mid-eighth century by members of a leading Bavarian noble family. It became one of the richest and most learned abbeys of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, with a celebrated scriptorium, and the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> romance Ruodlieb was probably written there in the eleventh century. It was secularised in 1803.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tegernsee-abbey.jpg" alt="Tegernsee Abbey" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schloss_Tegernsee.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
